Add or inspect components from this directory with the selected package manager:

    <<[ package_exec ]>> shadcn@<<[ shadcn_cli_version ]>> info
    <<[ package_exec ]>> shadcn@<<[ shadcn_cli_version ]>> add <component>

File-based routes live in `src/routes`. The TanStack Router Vite plugin watches them, generates `src/routeTree.gen.ts`, and automatically code-splits route components; run development or a bundle build after adding or renaming a route, and do not edit the generated tree directly. The index loader primes the shared TanStack Query cache before rendering, while Query owns freshness and the one-retry policy. The starter query passes its cancellation signal through both `/api/version` and `/health/ready` requests to the Vite proxy.

A full `scripts/jig dev` session supplies the current backend through `JIG_DEV_API_ORIGIN`, which takes precedence over an inherited generic override. For a direct Vite start or `scripts/jig dev --app <frontend-name>` against a separately managed backend, set `API_ORIGIN`. Replace the starter with the first product feature while keeping the tested API boundary or evolving it with the backend.

## End-to-end tests

From the repository root after bootstrap has installed dependencies, install the Chromium test browser once and run the package-local Playwright suite through the generated exact-package boundary:

    scripts/check-webapps.sh run-script <<[ frontend_dir ]>> test:e2e:install
    scripts/check-webapps.sh run-script <<[ frontend_dir ]>> test:e2e

Playwright starts Vite and the production Rust API on isolated loopback ports, waits for `/health/ready`, and verifies the browser-observed API response. Use `scripts/check-webapps.sh run-script <<[ frontend_dir ]>> test:e2e:ui` while authoring tests. Failure traces, screenshots, and the HTML report are written to ignored directories.

The defaults avoid the development database and are unique to this package. SQLite scaffolds reset the ignored `.agent/tmp/<<[ e2e_database_name ]>>.sqlite` and its `-shm`, `-wal`, and `-journal` sidecars before each run; Postgres scaffolds use `postgres://postgres:postgres@127.0.0.1:5432/<<[ e2e_database_name ]>>` and require a reachable disposable Postgres server. Set `E2E_DATABASE_URL` to use a different disposable database, `E2E_API_PORT` or `E2E_WEB_PORT` when the default ports are occupied (the API and web ports must differ), `E2E_SERVER_TIMEOUT_MS` for a slow cold Rust build, `E2E_GLOBAL_TIMEOUT_MS` to override the CI suite budget, or `E2E_BASE_URL` to test an already-running environment without starting local servers. The default CI suite budget includes both sequential local-server startup timeouts plus five minutes of test headroom, with a ten-minute minimum; the generated GitHub Actions job allows 30 minutes so dependency setup and installation remain outside that Playwright budget. PostgreSQL E2E uses its own Ubuntu runner because GitHub service containers require Linux; the scaffold workflow is project-owned after init if a self-hosted Linux label is preferred.
